# Per-profile API keys for services the agent drives (web-read broker, etc.).
#
# Copy this file to your profile's state dir as `secrets.env`:
#   cp sandbox_templates/common/secrets.env.template \
#      ~/.ai-sandbox/profiles/<profile>/secrets.env
# then fill in the keys you need and delete the lines you don't.
#
# `scripts/profile.sh <profile> up` also drops a `secrets.env.example` copy of
# this template into the profile dir for convenience.
#
# SECURITY / MECHANICS
#   * This file is injected as an OPTIONAL env_file (required: false) into the
#     agent container — same mechanism as db.env. profile.sh chmod 600s it.
#   * env_file is read only at container CREATE. After editing, recreate:
#       scripts/profile.sh <p> recreate
#     A plain `up` will NOT re-read this file for an already-running agent.
#   * Keys are read from the environment by the `webfetch` broker and never
#     appear on argv, so they stay out of the Bash-tool transcript and the
#     Squid URL log. Keep this file out of git — it lives under ~/.ai-sandbox,
#     outside the repo tree.
#   * Each service's HOST must be in proxy/allowed_domains.txt for the key to
#     be usable. Every broker backend's host is allowlisted in the [web-read]
#     block (Tavily, Firecrawl, TinyFish, Jina).
#   * VARIABLE NAMES ARE NOT A MATTER OF TASTE. Each one is whatever its
#     consumer actually reads; a plausible-looking synonym fails silently as a
#     missing key. Names below are cited to their call site — check there, not
#     the vendor's marketing copy, before renaming anything.

# --- Tavily (search + extract; api.tavily.com — already allowlisted) ---------
# Get a key at https://app.tavily.com/  (free tier available). Format: tvly-...
TAVILY_API_KEY=__SET_ME__

# --- TinyFish (search + fetch; api.search/api.fetch.tinyfish.ai — allowlisted
# [web-read]) — OPTIONAL --------------------------------------------------------
# Read by webfetch --via tinyfish (sandbox_templates/bin/webfetch). Search and
# Fetch are the vendor's free tier. The SAME key also unlocks their paid Agent
# and Browser APIs (a cloud browser the caller drives) — the broker never calls
# those and their hosts are not allowlisted; do not "connect" the TinyFish MCP
# inside a profile to get them. Get a key at https://agent.tinyfish.ai/api-keys
# Format: sk-tinyfish-...
# TINYFISH_API_KEY=sk-tinyfish-...

# --- Jina Reader (r.jina.ai / s.jina.ai — allowlisted [web-read]) — OPTIONAL -
# Read by webfetch --via jina (sandbox_templates/bin/webfetch). Keyless works
# (rate-limited); a key raises limits. Format: jina_...
# JINA_API_KEY=jina_...

# --- Firecrawl (api.firecrawl.dev — allowlisted [web-read]) — OPTIONAL -------
# Read by webfetch --via firecrawl (sandbox_templates/bin/webfetch). Note .dev,
# not .com. Format: fc-...
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=fc-...

# --- ClickUp personal API token — OPTIONAL -----------------------------------
# CLICKUP_TOKEN is the canonical name: it is what myclickup reads
# (src/myclickup/config.py, TOKEN_VAR). CLICKUP_API_TOKEN is accepted as a
# DEPRECATED alias; CLICKUP_API_KEY is wrong and reads as unset — that mistake
# was already made once and renamed out. ClickUp's own docs call this a
# personal API token, never a key. Format: pk_...
#
# Per-account variants CLICKUP_TOKEN_<ACCOUNT> (e.g. CLICKUP_TOKEN_ACME)
# take precedence when CLICKUP_ACCOUNT selects that account.
#
# Not needed for the claude.ai-hosted ClickUp MCP connector, which is OAuth and
# holds its own token. This is for the CLI/API client path only.
# CLICKUP_TOKEN=pk_...
